  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed dwelling would, by reason of its width and proximity to the eastern boundary of the site, appear as an narrow and visually cramped form of development that is at odds with the established local pattern of development along Devonshire Road. The proposed development would therefore be contrary to Policies 7, 10 and 26 of the Local Plan, Policy D4 of the London Plan as well as Policy DP3(1) of the NPPF.",
    "The proposed development would, by reason of the width and internal area of its single bedroom, result in a low quality design that would be to the detriment of future occupiers, contrary to the provisions of Policy D6 of the London Plan and Policies 7 and 10 of the Local Plan.",
    "The proposed development is considered to result in a poor parking space arrangement for the donor dwelling no. 49 Devonshire Road which is unlikely to be practically suitable for use by its occupants through obstruction to its parking area from a vehicle parked in front of the proposed dwelling, compromising day to day functionality and leading to a poor quality living environment and potential harm to the functioning of the highway, contrary to the provisions of Policy TR6 (4) of the NPPF, Policy D5 of the London Plan and Policies 7 and 24 of the Local Plan.",
    "In the event that this application is allowed through the appeals process, the proposals would be liable for the following CIL contributions:",
    "Mayoral CIL (MCIL2) contribution of £2,375 (x £25 per sqm).",
    "Havering CIL (HCIL) contribution of £11,875 (x £125 per sqm)",
    "Each contribution would be subject to indexation.",
    "Further details with regard to CIL are available from the Council's website.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy, notification of intended refusal and the reasons for it was given to the agent via email on 28/09/2026."
  ],
